<td id="S4.T6.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.38</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.40</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.42</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.40</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">0.38</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T6.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span title="Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct+Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct" class="ltx_glossaryref">V3LMA-Q-mini</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.36</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.30</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.22</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.18</td>
<td id="S4.T6.5.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.15</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the head weights, the results are shown in <a href="#S4.T6" title="In 4.1 Ablation study ‣ 4 Results ‣ V3LMA: Visual 3D-enhanced Language Model for Autonomous Driving" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. For the bigger models, the best performance is obtained when using a balanced weighting between the <span title="Large Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LLM</span>’s and <span title="Large Vision Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LVLM</span>’s head features. Nevertheless, the drop in performance is greater when the <span title="Large Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LLM</span> features are weighted above the <span title="Large Vision Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LVLM</span> ones.
On the other side, for the smaller Qwen combination the results indicate that the compressed visual features have a greater impact than the textual ones. In this case, for a heavier weighted <span title="Large Vision Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LVLM</span> features the difference is 21% with respect to heavier <span title="Large Language Model" class="ltx_glossaryref">LLM</span> features.</p>
</div>
